{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526696-just-how-dangerous-are-negation-men","id":1526696,"title":"Just how dangerous are Negation Men?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-12T03:00:43-08:00","id":1526696,"title":"Just how dangerous are Negation Men?","content":"For those unaware, Negation Men are a variant type of Marauder that's stuck in a permanent state of Denial rather than a permanent state of Madness, as would be the case for a typical Marauder. As such, Negation Men generate a \u201cCountermagick aura\u201d, automatically imposing Countermagick based on their Arete against any Effects in their immediate vicinity. They also count as Witnesses against Vulgar Magick. <br /> <br /> But is that all they do? I'd personally be inclined to allow them to develop Spheres, so long as they use their Magick to disrupt and conceal the supernatural. For example, I could see a Negation Man with Entropy inflicting Unbelief damage against fantastic beasts that <i>aren't </i>Bygones. An instinctive Mind effect might impose something like <b>Changeling</b>'s Mists on Sleepers in the vicinity, causing all but the most willful to forget the Magick they've seen or to rationalize it away. Prime could be used by a Negation Man to consume Quintessence that would otherwise be used to buttress Magickal Effects. And Spirit might be used to reinforce the Gauntlet, making it harder to summon spirits. <br /> <br /> In a crossover game, the Negation Man might prove dangerous to other supernatural types: similar to neutralizing Quintessence, I could see a Negation Man with Prime (and Entropy?) causing a vampire's Vitae to lose its effectiveness, and Entropy might cause low-Humanity vampires to be treated as Bygones; against werewolves, Life might interfere with shapeshifting and regeneration, while the aforementioned Spirit would interfere with Stepping Sideways, Mind might extend Delirium to people who would otherwise be immune and/or might lower someone's Willpower for the purpose of the effectiveness of Delirium, Prime (plus Spirit?) might disrupt the use of Rage and Gnosis; and Entropy (plus Spirit?) might cause a werewolf not in homid or lupus form to be treated as a Bygone and subjected to Unbelief. And so on. <br /> <br /> To what extent could this sort of thing be done using the normal rules for Willworking? And conversely, to what extent would this sort of thing either not be possible at all, or only be possible due to the Negation Man's unique status as a focus of Permanent Denial? <br /> <br /> And conversely, to what extent should Coincidental Magick be able to \u201cstill under the radar\u201d? As a Witness, a Negation Man should arguably impose the Domino Effect on Coincidental Magick that's nonetheless blatant enough to cause an observer to do a double-take due to unlikely coincidences happening too often. But as written, the Countermagick applies to Coincidental Magick as well as Vulgar Magick; should it? Or should Coincidental Effects not trigger the innate Countermagick? <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T08:07:33-07:00","id":1533699,"title":"","content":"As a fan of 'Blank' type characters, this is something I have toyed with in various splats but never got anything that I was really satisfied with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526696-just-how-dangerous-are-negation-men#post1526696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent could this sort of thing be done using the normal rules for Willworking? And conversely, to what extent would this sort of thing either not be possible at all, or only be possible due to the Negation Man's unique status as a focus of Permanent Denial?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like linking the effects to Spheres, this works well for a mechanical justification - the question is whether the negation effects are conscious efforts or reflexive, and maybe if the character is a PC or NPC. In most cases it might be easier to simply assign a difficulty increase for use of supernatural powers in proximity depending on the Sphere levels of the Negation Man (similar to the Anti-Psychic phenomena from Sorcerer) than having to roll through Countermagick effects. If the result is just inhibition of supernatural effects, it could be worth to take a shortcut here.<br /> <br /> Unmaking is another story and where it gets tricky. For most cases, suppressing a permanent effect should be more appropriate imo. Rather than dispelling the effects of vitae on a nearby vampire, I would probably inhibit the use of its properties- within narrative limits. I don't see an elder instantly turning to dust just because they bump into a Negation Man on their nightly hunt.<br /> This probably changes the moment they are directly confronted with something that conflicts with their focus. If it is something that is outside the limits of the Negation Man to change and conform with their focus, I would argue that they are likely to unconsciously manipulate <i>themselves</i> to perceive it as such, either by delusion or Magick.<br /> <br /> I would make a similar distinction for Coincidental Magick. If it is an ongoing effect that is subtle enough to not conflict with the focus of the Negation Man, no problem. If someone tries to cast a Coincidental effect while in the vicinity of one, it suffers from the increased difficulty of the passive 'negation aura'.<br /> <br /> An interesting case would be Negation Men inside the Technocratic Union, where their focus is likely to overlap with Consensus but still allows for Enlightened Science. I imagine they could go unnoticed for a long time and unwittingly sabotage some of their colleagues' work.<br /> And as someone who likes to cross over Mage and Werewolf, an obvious overlap point would be Drones. I could see Negation Men be susceptible to the One Song and attract the attention of the Weaver, although I don't think their Avatars would survive a conversion. Maybe? I actually don't remember how it works for Mages.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T11:13:05-07:00","id":1533711,"title":"","content":"More thoughts later. But for now, an Awakened Drone is limited to Coincidental Effects only. If we're going with MRev's notion that Marauders have portable Reality Zones, it would make sense for Blanks to always be limited to what their Focus defines as Coincidental. But then, what does it mean for a mage's Focus to define something as Coincidental? That basically means that the mage thinks it's <i>possible </i>\u2014 which in turn means that he'll only attempt it if it's something that would be Coincidental. <br /> <br /> So if a Marauder has a mobile Reality Zone, everything he does will be Coincidental by definition. If he <i>doesn't, </i>them you'll have the occasional awkwardness of a Blank in an RZ that defines something as Vulgar that he thinks should be possible. <br /> <br /> This may be one of those rare cases where the definition of \u201cjust what is an Earthly Foundation anyway?\u201d may actually matter; because if the Weaver defines Earthly Foundations, or conforms to them, them a Drone's restriction would be \u201ccan't do anything that an Earthly Foundation declares Vulgar\u201d, regardless of the Blank's own beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T03:29:57-07:00","id":1533742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526696-just-how-dangerous-are-negation-men?p=1533711#post1533711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, what does it mean for a mage's Focus to define something as Coincidental? That basically means that the mage thinks it's <i>possible </i>\u2014 which in turn means that he'll only attempt it if it's something that would be Coincidental.<br /> <br /> So if a Marauder has a mobile Reality Zone, everything he does will be Coincidental by definition. If he <i>doesn't, </i>them you'll have the occasional awkwardness of a Blank in an RZ that defines something as Vulgar that he thinks should be possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't this .. 'normal', for lack of a better word, for Marauders? When an effect isn't vulgar for <i>them</i>, the Paradox Backlash finds the next poor Awakened to hit. Or am I misunderstanding?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526696-just-how-dangerous-are-negation-men?p=1533711#post1533711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be one of those rare cases where the definition of \u201cjust what is an Earthly Foundation anyway?\u201d may actually matter; because if the Weaver defines Earthly Foundations, or conforms to them, them a Drone's restriction would be \u201ccan't do anything that an Earthly Foundation declares Vulgar\u201d, regardless of the Blank's own beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might even be more complex since the Weaver's goals are not congruent with Consensus at all. She is looking for Stasis and usually doesn't care too much about what is considered supernatural or vulgar as long as it doesn't conflict with her plan. So on top of the Foundations you probably have a bunch of rules that might seem pretty arbitrary to anyone outside the OneSong.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T06:42:10-07:00","id":1533744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526696-just-how-dangerous-are-negation-men?p=1533742#post1533742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't this .. 'normal', for lack of a better word, for Marauders? When an effect isn't vulgar for <i>them</i>, the Paradox Backlash finds the next poor Awakened to hit. Or am I misunderstanding?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misunderstanding. My point isn't that the Paradox gets shunted to someone else; it's that no Paradox would be generated in the first place. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526696-just-how-dangerous-are-negation-men?p=1533742#post1533742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might even be more complex since the Weaver's goals are not congruent with Consensus at all. She is looking for Stasis and usually doesn't care too much about what is considered supernatural or vulgar as long as it doesn't conflict with her plan. So on top of the Foundations you probably have a bunch of rules that might seem pretty arbitrary to anyone outside the OneSong.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. Basically, the Drone gains access to WeaverTech; but in exchange, loses the ability to cast Effects that the Weaver doesn't like. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}